1. What is distributed
----------------------

The project publishes source code. It may also publish container images:

  * the RENDERER image (default target of the Dockerfile): the Go binary
    `renderer`, the Templates and Configurations of this repository, and the
    Debian packages pandoc, librsvg2-bin, texlive-luatex, texlive-latex-base,
    texlive-latex-recommended and fonts-texgyre with their dependencies
    (about 175 Debian packages in total);
  * the INJECTOR image: the Go binary `injector` on gcr.io/distroless/static-debian13
    (no TeX toolchain, no shell, no package manager). The licences of the
    distroless base are in the image under /usr/share/doc; not verified in
    this run.

Not part of the release images: poppler-utils (installed only in the `golden`
and `sandbox` build stages, which are test images and are not published), the
sandbox probe, the Go toolchain, Node, Playwright and the dev stack images of
section 7.

The Debian packages are unmodified. They are an aggregate with the Go binary
in one image, not a combined program: the Worker starts `pandoc` and `lualatex`
as separate processes. See docs/research/license.md ("GPL FAQ recheck") for
the reasoning and the FAQ entries it rests on. Each component keeps its own
licence; the MIT licence of this project does not apply to them.


